d dragons</h2><p>East, South, West and North winds are honor tiles. Dragons are another honor category, often coordinated with the three suits in American play.</p></section><section><h2>Flowers and jokers</h2><p>Flowers are special tiles, while jokers have specific substitution rules. They play different roles and are not interchangeable.</p></section><section><h2>How many tiles?</h2><p>A typical American Mahjong set used in contemporary league-style play contains 152 tiles, including eight jokers. Check the set specification because other Mahjong variants and specialty sets differ.</p></section><section><h2>Shopping for a first set</h2><p>Before purchasing, check that a set supports American rules, includes the expected jokers and flowers, and fits your preferred racks and table size. You will also need a current annual card.</p></section><aside><strong>A note on official rules</strong><p>This is an independent educational overview, not a substitute for the current official National Mah Jongg League card or rules. We do not reproduce copyrighted annual card patterns.</p></aside><h2>Keep exploring</h2><div class="related"><a href="/">a →</a><a href="L">e →</a><a href="/">a →</a><a href="R">u →</a><a href="/#tools">Free tools →</a></div></main><footer>© {new Date().getFullYear()} My Mahjong Era · Independent American Mahjong learning and lifestyle</footer></body></html>